WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.450
- [Woman] This Great Big Story

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.640
was made possible by P&amp;G.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.273
Love over bias.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.910
(hip hop music)

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:12.100
- Battle rap is a competition.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.170
It's gladiator-style without the weapons.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:17.920
It's a verbal warfare.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.870
It gets ugly.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.080
But, it's the most entertaining thing

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.674
you will ever see in your life.

00:00:24.674 --> 00:00:27.424
(crowd cheering)

00:00:27.424 --> 00:00:30.020
(upbeat music)

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:31.810
My name is Sara Kana.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:34.080
I've been in battle rap
for over 30 years.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.990
I'm New York City born,

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:36.823
Bronx raised.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:42.270
Battle rap is one person versus
the other person with words,

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.300
and it's just a battle of wits.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.710
Of back-and-forth banter.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:50.060
One of the reasons I decided
to battle rap is because,

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.890
when you come from the
Bronx and you're a kid

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:52.900
and you're running the streets,

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:53.970
you're hip-hop's child,

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.423
and that's just what I am.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:02.520
Prism Battle League is the
only platform right now

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.210
currently concentrating
on opening the doors

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.883
for LGBTQ in battle rap.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:13.280
I started Prism Battle
League in January 2016

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.970
because there needed to be a platform

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:20.970
for lesbian, queer,
bisexual, transsexuals, gays,

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:24.890
whoever you are.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:29.000
Being LGBTQ and anything hip-
hop is usually frowned upon,

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.281
and Prism is changing that.

00:01:32.281 --> 00:01:35.560
(Tez rapping)

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.087
- I don't wanna hear, you know,

00:01:37.087 --> 00:01:38.797
“Oh, you're dope for a gay guy;

00:01:38.797 --> 00:01:40.110
"you got lyrics for a gay guy."

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.720
I just wanted you to hear the bars.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.330
Never take away my sexuality,

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:46.750
because I'm proud of who I
am at the end of the day,

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.700
but I want you to hear what I'm saying.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.560
Homophobia is real in hip-hop.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.880
Prism gives people a voice,

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.390
it gives people an option to speak out.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:56.793
It gives people a home.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:00.050
- My name's Philipe,

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.386
I've seen you since I was in high school.

00:02:02.386 --> 00:02:03.306
(Sara laughing)

00:02:03.306 --> 00:02:04.420
No, for real,

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:05.680
I used to watch Grind Time since, like,

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:06.513
the very beginning.

00:02:06.513 --> 00:02:07.930
It's nice to finally meet you.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:12.100
- One of the reasons why I
decided to self-fund Prism,

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.670
and why I'm so passionate,

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:16.840
is because I grew up
being a different person.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:20.240
And I'll never let nobody
do that to anybody there.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.960
People to this day look down on me,

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:24.810
and no matter how many
times they look down on me,

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:25.773
I rise above it.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.542
- Sara has definitely
guided me in the right path.

00:02:31.542 --> 00:02:33.090
She showed me, you know,

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.140
that you can do this,

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.790
and I am forever grateful to her.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.060
- When I was somebody from Prism Battle,

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.994
it's an overwhelming feeling,

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:44.040
almost like a mom feeling,

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.183
like, you know, these are my babies.

00:02:46.183 --> 00:02:50.070
Seeing these people get on
platforms they would never be on,

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.150
get the recognition they deserve,

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.273
I'll go broke before I let them down.

